 This is counting how many letters, the, the, the,

00:18:20.820 --> 00:18:22.500
 there's 16 thes and there's,

00:18:22.500 --> 00:18:25.340
 in that file there were six twos or whatever it was.

00:18:25.340 --> 00:18:26.180
 This is that code.

00:18:26.180 --> 00:18:27.940
 We'll get back to this code.

00:18:27.940 --> 00:18:30.300
 But what we've done here is I've added some comments

00:18:30.300 --> 00:18:33.700
 that are really for human consumption.

00:18:33.700 --> 00:18:36.020
 So this first paragraph is get the name of the file

00:18:36.020 --> 00:18:36.860
 and open it.

00:18:36.860 --> 00:18:39.780
 The second paragraph is count the word frequency.

00:18:39.780 --> 00:18:43.100
 You know, maybe I should have said histogram here.

00:18:43.100 --> 00:18:45.500
 Count the word frequency and assemble a histogram.

00:18:45.500 --> 00:18:48.140
 And then here I'm putting this pound sign in.

00:18:48.140 --> 00:18:49.940
 Find the most common word and then I'm all done.

00:18:49.940 --> 00:18:51.940
 I print this stuff out, right?

00:18:51.940 --> 00:18:56.120
 And so all I'm saying is comments are for people to read.

00:18:56.120 --> 00:18:58.660
 Your next programmer or the person who's gonna change

00:18:58.660 --> 00:19:01.300
 your program after you're done with it.

00:19:01.300 --> 00:19:02.140
 And they're nice.

00:19:02.140 --> 00:19:04.980
 And you don't have to use any particularly weird syntax

00:19:04.980 --> 00:19:06.820
 or variable naming conventions.

00:19:06.820 --> 00:19:09.740
 You put a pound sign in and you can write anything you want

00:19:09.740 --> 00:19:11.020
 from that point forward.

